WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.918
Edwina connects candidates, schools, trusts, Edwin consultants and Sub Vendors.

00:00:06.918 --> 00:00:13.836
This walkthrough follows actual prototype state changes using captured screens.

00:00:13.836 --> 00:00:17.865
People, routes and integrations are simulated.

00:00:17.865 --> 00:00:22.418
The candidate Today page now fits without scrolling.

00:00:23.618 --> 00:00:28.460
A school needs a Year Six maths teacher in Grimsby for nine.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.849
This sample represents a WhatsApp request.

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:38.789
Portal requests and a consultant logging a phone call enter the same booking workflow.

00:00:38.789 --> 00:00:42.097
Free text understanding is not connected.

00:00:43.297 --> 00:00:48.652
The shortlist is calculated from five thousand synthetic profiles.

00:00:48.652 --> 00:00:57.902
Verified experience, local travel, assignment checks, availability and arrival feasibility narrow the pool to two.

00:00:57.902 --> 00:01:04.475
This is a working rules demonstration, not a validated production matching model.

00:01:05.675 --> 00:01:13.441
Ben ranks ahead based on reviewed experience, previous trust assignments, sample feedback and travel.

00:01:13.441 --> 00:01:16.824
Open Why this match to inspect the evidence.

00:01:16.824 --> 00:01:24.129
Suitability is separate from readiness: neither candidate has yet confirmed they can leave now.

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:29.019
We introduce an outstanding screening task.

00:01:29.019 --> 00:01:34.081
Ben is directed to a proposed secure llama dot I D handoff.

00:01:34.081 --> 00:01:37.514
The demonstration collects no documents.

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:45.322
This is a proposed integration contract, subject to confirmation with Edwin’s product team.

00:01:46.522 --> 00:01:51.650
Completing that task leaves the screening outcome pending review.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:55.042
Ben is removed from the eligible shortlist.

00:01:55.042 --> 00:01:58.277
A strong match cannot override screening.

00:01:58.277 --> 00:02:03.247
Edwin must review the outcome before he becomes eligible again.

00:02:04.447 --> 00:02:11.249
After the reviewed screening outcome returns, Ben confirms he can leave within five minutes.

00:02:11.249 --> 00:02:15.611
He can choose the sample WhatsApp or candidate app channel.

00:02:15.611 --> 00:02:21.821
Calendar availability alone does not establish readiness for this urgent assignment.

00:02:23.021 --> 00:02:28.898
Ben now shows Ready now, with the confirmation time and WhatsApp source.

00:02:28.898 --> 00:02:34.121
His sample arrival includes departure time, travel and a buffer.

00:02:34.121 --> 00:02:38.202
In copilot mode, Sarah authorises the timed offer.

00:02:39.402 --> 00:02:44.365
Ben sees the same school, date, pay and arrival instructions.

00:02:44.365 --> 00:02:49.328
He acknowledges the briefing and accepts before the deadline.

00:02:49.328 --> 00:02:54.372
Sending an invitation is not treated as a confirmed placement.

00:02:55.572 --> 00:03:00.325
We deliberately simulate an unavailable Bullhorn connection.

00:03:00.325 --> 00:03:04.762
Ben has accepted, but the placement is not acknowledged.

00:03:04.762 --> 00:03:10.545
The booking remains pending and no final confirmation goes to the school.

00:03:10.545 --> 00:03:14.586
The consultant can see the failed integration step.

00:03:15.786 --> 00:03:20.370
After restoring the simulated connection, Sarah retries.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:25.937
Eligibility is checked again and the same correlation key is reused.

00:03:25.937 --> 00:03:28.885
One placement reference is recorded.

00:03:28.885 --> 00:03:33.060
Only then does the shared booking become confirmed.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:43.097
Helen now sees Ben confirmed for the eight forty-five arrival, with the agreed school charge and assignment assurance.

00:03:43.097 --> 00:03:47.515
Technical screening details and CRM errors stay with Edwin.

00:03:48.715 --> 00:03:52.116
Helen sends Ben the reception instructions.

00:03:52.116 --> 00:03:58.206
The recipient selector also offers Sarah at Edwin as a separate conversation.

00:03:58.206 --> 00:04:02.081
The message is attached to the confirmed booking.

00:04:03.281 --> 00:04:07.708
The same school message appears in Ben’s assignment view.

00:04:07.708 --> 00:04:15.552
This demonstrates a shared conversation across the two workspaces, rather than an isolated chat form.

00:04:16.752 --> 00:04:21.432
The trust can open the confirmed booking from its overview.

00:04:21.432 --> 00:04:27.224
Spend, budget, fill rate and school comparisons provide the broader view.

00:04:27.224 --> 00:04:35.396
Historical metrics remain a separate sample cohort; this one booking does not rewrite past performance.

00:04:36.596 --> 00:04:41.260
The trust can inspect weekly demand and a forecast scenario.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:49.500
The range is an assumption, not a statistical confidence interval or a live Department for Education feed.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:54.320
It illustrates the planning interface awaiting validated data.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:05:00.958
We reset the same matching scenario and choose exception-led handling.

00:05:00.958 --> 00:05:03.211
Sarah logs the school’s call.

00:05:03.211 --> 00:05:10.824
Edwina can now request readiness and send an eligible offer without separate consultant approvals.

00:05:12.024 --> 00:05:16.832
After Ben confirms readiness, the offer is sent automatically.

00:05:16.832 --> 00:05:23.037
The displayed counters track implemented workflow actions in this demonstration.

00:05:23.037 --> 00:05:26.759
They do not claim a measured staffing reduction.

00:05:27.959 --> 00:05:32.147
This time Ben does not accept before the deadline.

00:05:32.147 --> 00:05:34.157
The reservation expires.

00:05:34.157 --> 00:05:41.695
The updated clock makes Amelia’s arrival too late, so no direct educator remains eligible.

00:05:41.695 --> 00:05:46.553
Edwina releases the requirement to an approved Sub Vendor.

00:05:47.753 --> 00:05:55.668
Olivia proposes Eva for the same school requirement, confirms availability and submits sample evidence.

00:05:55.668 --> 00:06:00.509
Her charge to Edwin is separate from the school’s agreed price.

00:06:01.709 --> 00:06:07.851
The proposal remains in Evidence review with Edwin compliance as the next owner.

00:06:07.851 --> 00:06:10.691
It is not yet a confirmed assignment.

00:06:10.691 --> 00:06:16.603
Edwin reviews the evidence, then requests Eva’s own readiness and acceptance.

00:06:17.803 --> 00:06:22.328
Eva confirms she can arrive and receives the timed offer.

00:06:22.328 --> 00:06:27.487
Agency availability confirmation does not replace her acceptance.

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:32.408
She reads the same school briefing and accepts the assignment.

00:06:33.608 --> 00:06:40.247
The school now sees Eva confirmed in the same booking, at the unchanged school charge.

00:06:40.247 --> 00:06:44.415
It does not need a separate partner booking interface.

00:06:44.415 --> 00:06:49.278
Sourcing and internal purchasing remain Edwin responsibilities.

00:06:50.478 --> 00:06:56.230
Separately from the urgent booking, candidates can browse recommended roles.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:05.388
This example shows the date, gross pay, journey estimate and relevant experience before they decide to register interest.

00:07:06.588 --> 00:07:10.808
Registering interest is distinct from accepting an offer.

00:07:10.808 --> 00:07:15.991
The candidate sees that Sarah will review suitability with the school.

00:07:15.991 --> 00:07:24.802
The matching and integration flows remain prototypes, ready for product and operational validation before a live pilot.
